      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "Over the past ten years, laparoscopic surgery in the treatment of morbid obesity has expanded. However, there are few publications describing its side effects, notably the occurrence of gastric necrosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "OBSERVATION",
          "content": "Two years after laparoscopic-banding for morbid obesity, a case of acute gastroenteritis in a 45 Year-old woman proved to be a gastric necrosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "COMMENTS",
          "content": "Relatively unknown, this complication is generally revealed by non-specific clinical signs. Only emergency oeso-gastro-duodenal opacification permits diagnosis. Early diagnosis permits conservative treatment before the onset of necrosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Care must be taken when using this technique, which has not yet proved its innocuousness, and regular follow-up of the patient is crucial."
        }
      ]},
